<title>FRANCE: New York top destination for May ex-Paris aircargo.</title>
<headline>New York top destination for May ex-Paris aircargo.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top cargo export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in May 1997.</p>
<p>The top 10 destinations for ADP exports in May 1997 and, in</p>
<p>parentheses, the percentage change on May 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>  1.  New York		2,824  tonnes  (+1.8 percent)</p>
<p>  2.  Chicago		 2,345  tonnes  (+3.0)</p>
<p>  3.  Hong Kong	     2,249  tonnes (+25.1)</p>
<p>  4.  Tokyo		   1,805  tonnes  (-4.4)</p>
<p>  5.  Mexico City	   1,130  tonnes (+26.5)</p>
<p>  6.  Singapore		 905  tonnes (+33.8)</p>
<p>  7.  Montreal		  897  tonnes (-11.2)</p>
<p>  8.  Los Angeles	     759  tonnes (-31.1)</p>
<p>  9.  Miami		     747  tonnes  (-7.1)</p>
<p>  10. Sao Paulo		 700  tonnes (-22.7)</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
